{"slug":"scaling-drills","kind":"skill","topic":"math-proportional","intro":"<p>How does one quantity change when another is doubled, tripled or halved? Pick a relation, drag the factor and see the change: the picture and the bars resize as you go. Then practice: functional-dependence questions from the units you have reached, unit checks in kg, m and s, and SI conversions.</p>","howItWorksTitle":"Functional dependence in three steps","howItWorks":"<ol><li><b>Find the power.</b> Write the relation and read the power of the variable that changes: K = ½mv² has v², so K ∝ v². A square root is a power of ½ (T = 2π√(L/g), so T ∝ √L); a variable in the denominator has a negative power (F<sub>g</sub> ∝ 1/r²).</li><li><b>Raise the factor to that power.</b> If v triples, K changes by 3² = 9. If L is 4 times as long, T changes by √4 = 2. If r doubles, F<sub>g</sub> changes by 1/2² = ¼.</li><li><b>Multiply independent changes.</b> Double m and triple v: K changes by 2 × 9 = 18.</li></ol><p>Unit checks: write every quantity in kg, m and s (N = kg·m/s², J = kg·m²/s², W = kg·m²/s³, Pa = kg/(m·s²)) and add the powers. Conversions: an area converts with the square of the length factor and a volume with its cube (1 m³ = 10⁶ cm³).</p><p>Factors count within about 1%; conversions within 0.6%.</p>","contexts":[{"id":"math-units","topic":"math-units","types":["units","convert"],"exprs":["dt","dvdt","rho","lw"],"convs":["kmh","g","cm","mm","cm2","cm3","gcm3","min","L","kN"]},{"id":"math-proportional","topic":"math-proportional","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["square","cube","circle","trip","rect"]},{"id":"motion-representations","topic":"motion-representations","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["fromrest","vat"],"exprs":["halfat2"]},{"id":"motion-2d","topic":"motion-2d","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["droptime","range"]},{"id":"second-law","topic":"second-law","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["newton"],"exprs":["ma"]},{"id":"gravitational-force","topic":"gravitational-force","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["gravity","surfaceg"]},{"id":"spring-forces","topic":"spring-forces","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["spring"],"exprs":["kx"]},{"id":"circular-motion","topic":"circular-motion","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["centripetal"],"exprs":["v2r"]},{"id":"kinetic-energy","topic":"kinetic-energy","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["ke"],"exprs":["halfmv2"]},{"id":"potential-energy","topic":"potential-energy","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["pespring","pegrav"],"exprs":["mgh","halfkx2"]},{"id":"power","topic":"power","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["power"],"exprs":["fv","wt"]},{"id":"linear-momentum","topic":"linear-momentum","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["momentum"],"exprs":["mv"]},{"id":"impulse","topic":"impulse","types":["factor","units"],"relations":["impulse"],"exprs":["ft"]},{"id":"torque","topic":"torque","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["torque"]},{"id":"rotational-inertia","topic":"rotational-inertia","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["inertia"],"exprs":["mr2"]},{"id":"rotational-kinetic-energy","topic":"rotational-kinetic-energy","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["rotke"]},{"id":"orbits","topic":"orbits","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["orbitv"]},{"id":"shm-period","topic":"shm-period","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["pendulum","springT"],"exprs":["pend","springT"]},{"id":"shm-energy","topic":"shm-energy","types":["factor","combo"],"relations":["shmE"]},{"id":"fluid-pressure","topic":"fluid-pressure","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["pressure"],"exprs":["rhogh","fa"]},{"id":"buoyancy","topic":"buoyancy","types":["factor","combo","units"],"relations":["buoyant"],"exprs":["rhovg"]},{"id":"fluid-flow","topic":"fluid-flow","types":["factor","units"],"relations":["continuity","torricelli"],"exprs":["av","sqrt2gh"]}],"live":true,"units":{